    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "QU7tM",
      "x": 1560,
      "y": 86480,
      "name": "146 · Graph · Node Selected · Light",
      "context": "LOREKEEPER-500 graph with a node selected. Selecting narrows the graph to the node and its direct links, so nothing on the canvas is dimmed - everything left is related. The selected node is marked by a two-layer ring alone (a background-colour band, then a bright line); its name keeps the same weight as every other label. The ring is two layers because the brightest node colour equals color-text-primary and a single-layer ring would vanish on a character node. The right panel is a list of node boxes - the selected node first, then every node directly linked to it - each carrying a kind icon, the file name on one line, a relation chip naming the selected node it is linked to, and the file's description clamped to two lines. The chip carries the linked node's name only, not the property that made the link. Manuscripts have no description property, so those boxes drop the line. The selected node's box is marked only by a 2px achromatic rule on the left. The box itself opens the file; there is no separate open-file button and no counts are shown.",
      "theme": {
        "b:mode": "light"
      },
      "clip": true,
      "width": 1440,
      "height": 900,
      "fill": "$b:color-bg-canvas",
      "stroke": "$b:color-border-default",
